From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phpv patch conversion <patches@phpv.invalid>
Subject: [0001-configure-curl-cflags] PHP 7.0's generated configure clobbers CFLAGS during the 'checking for openssl support in libcurl' test with `curl-config --cflags` output (just an -I path).

PHP 7.0's generated configure clobbers CFLAGS during the 'checking for
openssl support in libcurl' test with `curl-config --cflags` output
(just an -I path). The conftest uses strncasecmp() without <strings.h>,
a hard error on GCC 14+; append warning-suppression flags to the
substitution so the test compiles clean.

---
diff --git a/a/php-7.0.33/configure b/b/php-7.0.33/configure
index bedb958..12b271b 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -23835,7 +23835,7 @@ $as_echo "#define HAVE_CURL_SSL 1" >>confdefs.h
 
 
     save_CFLAGS="$CFLAGS"
-    CFLAGS="`$CURL_CONFIG --cflags`"
+    CFLAGS="`$CURL_CONFIG --cflags` -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration"
     save_LDFLAGS="$LDFLAGS"
     LDFLAGS="`$CURL_CONFIG --libs`"
 
